Kamen Fight - Project DocumentationKamen Fight is a Web-based, turn-based Kamen Rider fighting game built with vanilla JavaScript, HTML5 Video, and CSS3. 
The game features simultaneous command selection, directional charge mechanics, sequential video-driven combat resolution, smart AI decision engines, batch match simulation, and full mirror-match support.
Key FeaturesDirectional Charge System: Players hold directional keys (A, D, W, S) to build charge percentage before confirming attacks with action keys (J, K, L, I). 
Charge percentage dynamically scales damage, accuracy, and guard success.
Special Guard (A+I) omni-blocks attacks, while mismatched guards lead to full damage and action interruption.
Chi & Faint Mechanics: Resource pool caps at 16 Chi with active Full Power (>14 Chi) and Low Power (<5 Chi) modifiers. Accumulating 100 Faint points stuns the target into a 1-turn forced idle state.


├── index.html              # Main game layout and media containers
├── css/
│   └── style.css           # Styling, HUD layout, floating popups, video scaling
├── data/
│   ├── moves.json          # Move definitions, Chi costs, damage ratios, video mappings
│   └── riders.json         # Roster list, maximum LP, sprite icon bindings
├── js/
│   ├── common.js           # Shared combat parameters, charge thresholds, helpers
│   ├── combat_engine.js    # Turn resolution, guard calculations, faint buildup
│   ├── cpu_controller.js   # CPU charge manager
│   ├── foresee_engine.js   # Minimax / Expectimax 3-turn tree search
│   ├── ai.js               # Memory store, habit tracking, AI profiles
│   ├── game.js             # Core battle initialization and match state management
│   ├── match_manager.js    # Round countdown, input handlers, action confirmation
│   ├── media.js            # Center cutscene player and video duration handlers
│   ├── simulator.js        # Synchronized headless batch simulation engine
│   ├── ui.js               # HUD rendering and floating text popups
│   └── vs_select.js        # Character select screen, BGM, simulation modal UI
└── assets/
    ├── sounds/             # BGM tracks (matchup.mp3, matchup1.mp3)
    ├── images/icons/       # Rider thumbnails
    └── videos/             # Rider video clips (idle.mp4, faint.mp4, etc.)


Setup & Deployment InstructionsLocal Execution: 
Clone or download the repository folder and open index.html directly in any modern Web browser (Chrome, Firefox, Edge, Safari). No build steps or server dependencies required.

GitHub Pages Deployment: 
Push the repository to GitHub and enable GitHub Pages under Settings > Pages. 
Asset Naming Warning: Ensure all asset paths and video filenames inside assets/videos/<rider_id>/ are strictly lowercase (e.g., idle.mp4, guard.mp4) to prevent 404 errors on Linux host servers.

